# GMEOW Ontology Documentation

Version **16**.

This site documents **6476** vocabulary terms across **85** slices.

## I want to…

- [Model Contested or Attributed Facts](recipes/contested-or-attributed-facts/index.md) — Keep incompatible claims side by side by recording standpoint, vantage, modality, and evidence on the claim rather than on a single global fact slot\.
- [Publish Documents for Schema\.org Consumers](recipes/documents-and-schema-org/index.md) — Start with native document and web\-presence facts, then inspect which facts project to schema\.org and where projection is lossy\.
- [Model Events and Participants](recipes/events-and-participants/index.md) — Describe an event, participant roles, time, place, and source evidence without collapsing participation into a flat string\.
- [Model Graph\-RAG Dataset Lineage](recipes/graph-rag-dataset-lineage/index.md) — Connect sources, chunks, extracted entities, evidence spans, and pipeline provenance so retrieval artifacts remain auditable\.
- [Describe Offline GTS Distribution](recipes/offline-gts-distribution/index.md) — Treat a GTS file as a first\-class graph object with segments, profiles, chain heads, opaque frames, codecs, and compaction lineage\.
- [Model Person Names Without a Preferred\-Name Slot](recipes/person-names-and-display/index.md) — Represent coexisting names, pronouns, aliases, usage contexts, and display suppression without asserting one global winner\.
- [Audit AI and Graph\-RAG Pipelines](learning-paths/audit-ai-or-graph-rag/index.md) — Connect generated claims to source chunks, evidence spans, tools, model context, and provenance before consumers see them\.
- [Model a Contested or Attributed Claim](learning-paths/model-a-contested-claim/index.md) — Represent claims by vantage and evidence rather than overwriting facts into a single global truth slot\.
- [Model a Person Without Flattening Identity](learning-paths/model-a-person/index.md) — Start with a person, add names and contact points, then keep authority links and display choices separate from identity\.
- [Publish Web Structured Data](learning-paths/publish-web-structured-data/index.md) — Model documents, events, people, and organizations natively, then inspect which fields project cleanly to broad consumers\.
- [Ship Offline GTS Documentation](learning-paths/ship-offline-gts-docs/index.md) — Treat the distribution file, embedded docs, profiles, segments, codecs, and lineage as first\-class graph facts\.
- [RDF\-to\-developer glossary](glossary/index.md) — a bridge for readers new to RDF.

